<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,479,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,479,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 01/08/97    01/01/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 30,479,000  30,543,000-R  28,032,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 163,820     161,439	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	34,948,000  34,948,000    33,569,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,140,728  35,140,728	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised from 30,579,000  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   01/08/97    01/01/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   5,399,000   5,344,000     4,880,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    4,968,000   5,172,000     4,474,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  5,174,000   5,197,000*    5,013,000</p>
<p> South Central    3,326,000   3,339,000     2,749,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  4,146,000   4,208,000     3,653,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,376,000   5,450,000     5,340,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  2,090,000   1,835,000     1,923,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	30,479,000  30,543,000**  28,032,000</p>
<p>*Revised from 5,233,000  **Revised from 30,579,000</p>
